course: dictionary
lesson: 11297
title: One word, three meanings: yang
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word yang is a good example. In «Yang Liwei became China's first astronaut in 2003», Yang is a name, because it has a capital letter and comes before a person's given name, Liwei.
explain: In the old Chinese idea of yin and yang, yang is one half of a pair of opposite forces that balance each other. Yang is the bright, warm, active side, and yin is the dark, cool, quiet side. Here yang is a common noun, and it has no capital letter because it is not a name.
explain: In Mandarin, yáng is a word in its own right, not an English word. It can mean sun, as in tàiyáng, or sheep, depending on its tone and character. Because it comes from another language, the context and your teacher's notes are your best clues.
fact: Yang has three meanings: a philosophy idea, a Mandarin word, and a surname.
fact: Yin and yang is shown as a circle with a black and a white swirl, each with a dot of the other colour. This means opposites belong together.
fact: Yang is a common Chinese surname, so «Yang Liwei» is the name of a person.
fact: Yang Liwei became China's first astronaut in 2003, and China was the third country to send people to space on its own rockets.
fact: Mandarin yáng can sound like «yahng» to an English ear, and its tone changes its meaning.
exercise: In «Yang Liwei became China's first astronaut in 2003», what kind of word is Yang? | The bright, warm half of a balance of two forces | *A surname, the name of a person | A sheep in the Chinese zodiac | A sun or sunshine in Chinese
exercise: In yin and yang, what does yang stand for? | A dark, cold, quiet side | A kind of Chinese sheep | A tall building in China | *The bright, warm, active side that balances yin
exercise: In «even China's astronaut Yang Liwei said he could not see it from orbit», how do you know Yang is a name? | It is a sheep in the zodiac | It means sun, as in tàiyáng | It comes after the word astronaut in every sentence | *It has a capital letter and comes before the given name Liwei
test: In a yin and yang picture, what does a dot of the other colour show? | That one colour is more important | *That opposites belong together | That the picture is finished | A mistake in the drawing
test: Which word means the sun in Mandarin? | yin | *tàiyáng | orbit | Liwei
exam: Yang has more than one meaning, so how can a reader tell which one is meant? | Ask a friend to read the text aloud | Skip the word and never come back to it | *Look at the context: the capital letter, the nearby words and the topic of the text | Guess the first meaning in the dictionary and stop reading
